{"name":"Bondi","hex":"#16698c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bondi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Sydney, New South Wales, Australia.","A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bondi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bondi, New South Wales","blocks":[{"text":"Bondi is a suburb of eastern Sydney, in the state of New South Wales, Australia, seven kilometres east of the Sydney central business district, in the local government area of Waverley Council."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bondi%2C_New_South_Wales","wikidata":"Q892238"},{"title":"Bondi Beach","blocks":[{"text":"Bondi Beach is a beach and the surrounding suburb in Sydney, New South Wales, Australia. Bondi Beach is located 7 kilometres east of the Sydney central business district, in the local government area of Waverley Council, in the Eastern Suburbs. In the 2021 Australian census it had a population of 11,513 residents. Its postcode is 2026. Bondi, North Bondi and Bondi Junction are neighbouring suburbs. Bondi Beach is one of the most visited tourist sites in Australia, and the location of two television series, Bondi Rescue and Bondi Vet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Bondi_from_above.jpg/330px-Bondi_from_above.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bondi_Beach","wikidata":"Q673418"},{"title":"Bondi (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Bondi or Bondy is a surname. Notable people with the surname include:"},{"items":["August Bondi (1833–1907), Austrian-American abolitionist","Beulah Bondi (1888–1981), American actress","Curt W. Bondy (1894–1972), German psychologist and social educator","Egon Bondy, born Zbyněk Fišer (1930–2007), Czech philosopher and poet","François Bondy (1915–2003), Swiss journalist and novelist","Hermann Bondi (1919–2005), Anglo-Austrian mathematician and physicist","John Adrian Bondy, British-Canadian mathematician","Jonas Bondi (1804–1874), German-American rabbi and newspaper editor","Joseph Bondy (1863–1945), American lawyer, politician, and military officer","Luc Bondy (1948–2015), Swiss theater and opera director","Pam Bondi, United States Attorney General (2025–2026)","Renato Rafael Bondi, Brazilian footballer","Simon Bondi (1774–1816), lexicographer","Vic Bondi, of American band Articles of Faith","William Bondy (1870–1964), a longtime federal judge of the Southern District of New York","Yak Bondy, American music producer","Bondy, a pseudonym of Gene Bilbrew (1923–1974), American cartoonist and fetish artist"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bondi_(name)","wikidata":"Q20064399"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg/500px-Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg/1280px-Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg/500px-Bondi_ice_bergs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABondi_ice_bergs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bondi_Post_Office.jpg/120px-Bondi_Post_Office.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bondi_Post_Office.jpg/250px-Bondi_Post_Office.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Bondi_Post_Office.jpg/120px-Bondi_Post_Office.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABondiBuilding9.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi